= Carve Feature Demo

%% This file demonstrates Carve 0.2. Comments do not render.

A document with the core constructs in one place. Edit a line to see the preview and the four output views change.

== Headings and attributes

{#section .featured}
=== A heading with an id and a class

A heading may also use `#` markers in place of `=`; the Format button rewrites them to `=`:

```carve
{#setup .lead}
## Setup
```

== Inline formatting

Use /emphasis/, *strong text*, {_underline_}, {~strike~}, and {=highlight=}.
Use `inline code`, H{,2,}O and x{^2^}. An escaped * is literal.

An [inline link](https://example.com), an <https://example.com> autolink, and a reference [link][site] all work.
A cross-reference points to </#section>.

[site]: https://example.com "Reference definition"

An image can carry alt text and a caption:

![A simple diagram](images/diagram.png)
^ Figure #: A diagram in the documentation.

A raw inline span can contain `<kbd>Enter</kbd>`{=html}; it remains escaped while raw HTML is off.
Editorial marks can show {+inserted words+} and {-deleted words-}.

